(5. CONFIDENTIALITY AND NON-DISCLOSURE) '
/F2 9.5 Tf
(5.1 Definition. "Confidential Information" means all non-public technical, business,) '
/F1 8.5 Tf
(customer, or financial data disclosed by one Party to the other, marked as) '
/F1 8.5 Tf
(confidential or reasonably understood to be confidential.) '
/F2 9.5 Tf
(5.2 Obligations. The receiving Party agrees: \(a\) to hold Confidential Information in) '
/F1 8.5 Tf
(strict confidence; \(b\) not to disclose it to third parties without prior written) '
/F1 8.5 Tf
(consent; and \(c\) to use it solely for executing this Agreement.) '
/F2 9.5 Tf
(5.3 Exclusions. Confidentiality obligations do not apply to information that: \(a\) is) '
/F1 8.5 Tf
(or becomes public knowledge without breach; \(b\) was already known to the recipient) '
/F1 8.5 Tf
(prior to disclosure; or \(c\) is required to be disclosed by valid court subpoena.) '
/F2 9.5 Tf
(5.4 Survival. Confidentiality obligations shall survive termination of this Agreement) '
/F1 8.5 Tf
(for a period of five \(5\) years.) '
/F1 8.5 Tf
() '
